# =============================================================================
# PharmaRidge — production .gitignore
# =============================================================================
# Rule of thumb: ignore anything that is (a) regenerable, (b) machine-specific,
# or (c) a secret. Everything a fresh clone needs to build and deploy MUST stay
# tracked — including package-lock.json (see the note in the Dependencies
# section; this was previously ignored by mistake).

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and credentials  — NEVER commit these
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Wrangler's local secret file. Holds JWT_SECRET for `wrangler dev`. A leaked
# JWT secret lets anyone mint a valid token for any role, including ADMIN.
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*
!.dev.vars.example

# Generic env files. Not used by the Worker (Cloudflare secrets are used
# instead) but listed so a future script or tool cannot leak one by accident.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Cloudflare API tokens / CLI credentials, if a token is ever written locally.
.cloudflare/
wrangler.toml.local
*.pem
*.key
!public/**/*.key

# Anything a developer names like a credential dump.
*credentials*
*secrets*
!**/secrets.example.*

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.npm/
.pnpm-store/
.yarn/
jspm_packages/

# package-lock.json IS TRACKED ON PURPOSE.
# It pins the exact dependency tree (hono, wrangler and their transitive deps)
# so a deploy six months from now installs byte-identical packages. Ignoring it
# — as this file previously did — means `npm install` can silently pull a new
# minor version of a dependency between a tested build and a production deploy,
# which is precisely the class of "it worked yesterday" failure a pharmacy
# cannot afford. Do not add it back to this list.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cloudflare / Wrangler build + local state
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local D1 database, KV/R2 emulation, build cache. Regenerated by
# `wrangler d1 migrations apply --local`. Committing it would ship one
# developer's test data — including demo PIN hashes — to every clone.
# NOTE the two forms. `.wrangler/` (trailing slash) matches a DIRECTORY only.
# In sandboxes we relocate this state outside the snapshotted tree and leave a
# SYMLINK named `.wrangler` in its place — a symlink is not a directory, so the
# slash form does not match it and git offered to commit the link itself. A
# committed symlink pointing at one machine's ~/.cache would break every fresh
# clone. The slashless form below covers both the real dir and the symlink.
.wrangler
.wrangler/
.mf/
dist/
build/
.output/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated data files
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# worker/seed.sql is GENERATED by `npm run db:generate-seed` (generate-seed.js)
# and contains freshly-hashed demo PINs and random UUIDs. It differs on every
# run, so committing it produces meaningless diffs — and it is demo data that
# must never reach a real client deployment.
#
# NOTE: worker/migrations/*.sql is deliberately NOT ignored. Migrations —
# including 0002_nafdac_catalog.sql (the 6,801-product NAFDAC reference table)
# — are schema and must ship with the repo.
worker/seed.sql
worker/live-sample-reset.sql
worker/first-admin.sql
worker/client-admin-reset.sql
worker/schema-admin-format.sql
worker/schema-admin-restore.sql

# Database exports / backups produced by `wrangler d1 export`. These contain
# REAL CLIENT DATA — patient prescriptions, buyer IDs from the controlled-drug
# register, staff records. They must never enter version control.
backup-*.sql
*.dump.sql
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
!worker/migrations/*.sql

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs and diagnostics
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*
report.*.json

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test / coverage artefacts
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
coverage/
.nyc_output/
*.lcov
test-results/
playwright-report/
.vitest/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and IDEs
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.example.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.project
.classpath
.settings/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Operating systems
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Windows is the primary deployment workstation for this project
# (see DEPLOY-MULTI-CLIENT-SSH-CLOUDFLARE-WINDOWS.md), so these matter in practice.
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.lnk

# macOS
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*

# Linux
.directory
.Trash-*
.nfs*

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Temporary / scratch
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
tmp/
temp/
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
tmp_*.js
*-preview.html

# Derived visual-inspection artefacts from the deterministic icon builder.
# The SVG source is build-icons.js itself; these raster/vector previews are
# regenerated by `npm run assets:icons` and are not application runtime assets.
worker/test/tools/icon-source.svg
public/icons/icon-source-frameless.png

# Large source data kept out of the repo. The NAFDAC Greenbook JSON export
# (~22 MB) is the INPUT to tools/build-nafdac-catalog.js; the generated
# migration is what ships. Keeping the raw export out avoids bloating every
# clone with a file only the catalog rebuild needs.
greenbook*.json
nafdac-raw*.json
uploads/

